WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:23.583 --> 00:00:25.041
Hooray!

2
00:01:03.125 --> 00:01:04.083
Good morning.

3
00:01:10.291 --> 00:01:13.083
I can't believe you didn't even touch me.

4
00:01:13.666 --> 00:01:17.625
How did you even fall asleep?
with this face and body next to you?

5
00:01:17.708 --> 00:01:19.916
You said there wouldn't be a second time.

6
00:01:21.333 --> 00:01:24.375
Yes, but who listens to such prohibitions?

7
00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:29.208
If that's what you wanted.

8
00:01:32.083 --> 00:01:33.166
You're sleeping with someone.

9
00:01:35.208 --> 00:01:36.500
NO.

10
00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:41.583
Are you angry that I left without saying a word?

11
00:01:46.708 --> 00:01:48.500
How would you put it?

12
00:01:50.041 --> 00:01:53.041
I haven't slept well since that day.

13
00:01:54.583 --> 00:01:56.541
Maybe you are my sleeping pill?

14
00:01:57.625 --> 00:02:00.875
Even if how could you sleep
and do nothing?

15
00:02:01.708 --> 00:02:04.375
The food is getting cold.

16
00:02:10.458 --> 00:02:11.875
Sorry,

17
00:02:11.958 --> 00:02:14.583
but I don't usually eat breakfast.

18
00:02:19.333 --> 00:02:20.375
Pride!

19
00:02:27.125 --> 00:02:29.833
Don't look at me with that face
"you're so sweet."

20
00:02:29.916 --> 00:02:31.375
Was I making that face?

21
00:02:31.875 --> 00:02:32.791
Yes.

22
00:02:34.541 --> 00:02:37.083
What is this significant look?

23
00:02:37.166 --> 00:02:38.333
Don't worry.

24
00:02:39.125 --> 00:02:41.125
I can't fall more in love with you.

25
00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:43.666
You're following orders again.

26
00:02:44.625 --> 00:02:46.500
Nice guys are repulsive.

27
00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:48.708
Try this.

28
00:03:06.375 --> 00:03:07.375
Wait!

29
00:03:09.166 --> 00:03:11.708
Thanks for the meal.
But we won't meet again.

30
00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:13.791
No, wait. Wait a minute!

31
00:03:15.833 --> 00:03:18.875
Why did I go to him at all?

32
00:03:18.958 --> 00:03:20.916
All right. Please go.

33
00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.041
Your coat!

34
00:03:23.125 --> 00:03:24.291
Coat!

35
00:03:50.083 --> 00:03:51.583
ROMANTICS ANONYMOUS

36
00:03:51.666 --> 00:03:54.875
EPISODE 3
WASABI EN SOIE

37
00:03:54.958 --> 00:03:56.500
RAINBOW PALETTE ON SALE

38
00:03:56.583 --> 00:03:57.583
Good morning.

39
00:03:57.666 --> 00:03:58.833
Looks nice.

40
00:04:03.375 --> 00:04:05.083
Maybe I'll take it.

41
00:04:08.583 --> 00:04:10.208
Good morning.

42
00:04:11.833 --> 00:04:14.291
And what do people write in surveys?

43
00:04:14.375 --> 00:04:15.291
I'm telling you now.

44
00:04:15.375 --> 00:04:17.375
After the return of the Rainbow Palette

45
00:04:17.458 --> 00:04:21.583
even Futago Sweets got complaints.

46
00:04:21.666 --> 00:04:24.541
"I regret buying wasabi chocolate."

47
00:04:25.041 --> 00:04:27.125
“The wasabi chocolate was terrible.”

48
00:04:27.708 --> 00:04:31.750
“I bought wasabi chocolate by mistake
due to bad marking.

49
00:04:31.833 --> 00:04:34.125
“Can I get a refund?”

50
00:04:35.125 --> 00:04:38.833
They bought the Rainbow Palette
and found a chocolate with wasabi inside.

51
00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:43.500
They did not know its contents
and they got an unpleasant surprise.

52
00:04:43.583 --> 00:04:46.916
They didn't know the content?
It's written on the package.

53
00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:49.625
Not many people read this
when they buy the set.

54
00:04:50.458 --> 00:04:52.958
Additionally, wasabi prices are rising,

55
00:04:53.041 --> 00:04:55.541
so suppliers demand higher prices.

56
00:04:56.375 --> 00:05:00.416
As you can see,
It doesn't sell well on its own either.

57
00:05:03.208 --> 00:05:04.291
What does the office say?

58
00:05:05.041 --> 00:05:08.333
“Too many complaints and low margin.”

59
00:05:08.416 --> 00:05:10.916
They told us to stop production.

60
00:05:12.666 --> 00:05:14.083
Thank you for your patience.

61
00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:19.416
Here's the note with the number.

62
00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:20.791
Thank you.

63
00:05:28.958 --> 00:05:30.000
What?

64
00:05:30.083 --> 00:05:36.208
Why do you want to do something so difficult
like chocolate with wasabi?

65
00:05:36.291 --> 00:05:40.708
Well, wasabi is not a product
intended to be eaten separately.

66
00:05:40.791 --> 00:05:45.666
If you use too much,
you're asking for a disaster.

67
00:05:46.333 --> 00:05:49.708
But keep the right balance

68
00:05:49.791 --> 00:05:54.125
and will create a unique taste with which
no other ingredient compares.

69
00:05:55.125 --> 00:05:59.666
Even when he's hiding, he does a great job.

70
00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:00.958
I see.

71
00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:07.583
It's similar to you, Hana.

72
00:06:07.666 --> 00:06:08.625
To me?

73
00:06:08.708 --> 00:06:10.083
Is he like me?

74
00:06:10.166 --> 00:06:12.166
I just wish

75
00:06:12.250 --> 00:06:18.125
to go out to people a little more often.

76
00:06:19.833 --> 00:06:21.250
To the people, right?

77
00:06:21.333 --> 00:06:23.291
Yes, that's what I'm counting on.

78
00:06:28.458 --> 00:06:30.750
It's true that the price of wasabi has increased,

79
00:06:30.833 --> 00:06:33.916
but we rarely use it here.

80
00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:36.041
Oh. I can?

81
00:06:36.125 --> 00:06:38.083
From what I see in the room,

82
00:06:38.166 --> 00:06:40.583
is popular with foreign tourists.

83
00:06:40.666 --> 00:06:41.875
Right!

84
00:06:42.458 --> 00:06:45.083
Even KitKat wafers
they taste like wasabi, right?

85
00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:50.083
Apart from tourists, what are the customers?

86
00:06:50.166 --> 00:06:52.541
do they buy single Wasabi en Soie?

87
00:06:54.750 --> 00:06:57.666
I should ask those
who know best.

88
00:06:58.166 --> 00:07:03.375
Does anyone here think Wasabi en Soie
is the best it can be?

89
00:07:10.625 --> 00:07:14.458
So maybe let's work together?

90
00:07:14.541 --> 00:07:16.458
Especially the confectioners.

91
00:07:17.833 --> 00:07:21.000
Is there any way
to improve the recipe?

92
00:07:22.375 --> 00:07:26.458
What do you think, boss?

93
00:07:29.916 --> 00:07:31.583
I…

94
00:07:34.916 --> 00:07:37.916
I always believed
that Kenji's recipe was perfect.

95
00:07:38.958 --> 00:07:42.708
For me the current taste is the best.

96
00:07:47.750 --> 00:07:51.708
If you don't want to change it,
we have to stop individual sales.

97
00:07:56.666 --> 00:07:59.166
Good job. See you tomorrow.

98
00:08:00.416 --> 00:08:01.958
See you.

99
00:08:07.875 --> 00:08:10.958
You wanted to speak in front of people,
but you couldn't.

100
00:08:11.791 --> 00:08:12.916
Gosh.

101
00:08:13.416 --> 00:08:15.541
This is a big step forward.

102
00:08:15.625 --> 00:08:19.291
How is this possible if I failed?

103
00:08:19.375 --> 00:08:22.583
You failed because you tried.

104
00:08:22.666 --> 00:08:26.291
And this test is proof that
that you wanted something more.

105
00:08:27.083 --> 00:08:30.625
Before, you didn't want to at all
find yourself in such a situation.

106
00:08:31.125 --> 00:08:33.250
Maybe you're right.

107
00:08:33.750 --> 00:08:38.875
Does this mean I'm slowly getting better?

108
00:08:40.333 --> 00:08:44.416
Of course. You even alluded to it
eye contact and showed empathy?

109
00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:45.958
Yes.

110
00:08:46.041 --> 00:08:49.916
Physical symptoms do not go away
from day to day.

111
00:08:50.416 --> 00:08:54.291
But your heart
I want to change, Darth Vader.

112
00:08:54.791 --> 00:08:57.500
You just need to practice step by step.

113
00:09:00.541 --> 00:09:02.000
Exercise…

114
00:09:02.083 --> 00:09:05.041
Give yourself a high rating.

115
00:09:05.125 --> 00:09:07.625
You have successfully emerged into the outside world.

116
00:09:08.625 --> 00:09:10.208
Thanks to the boss

117
00:09:10.708 --> 00:09:15.125
even wasabi like me
can come out into the world.

118
00:09:54.458 --> 00:09:55.375
What?

119
00:10:06.375 --> 00:10:11.125
Thank you for contacting me regarding your problems
with wasabi chocolates

120
00:10:11.208 --> 00:10:13.833
and ideas for their improvement.

121
00:10:13.916 --> 00:10:15.250
I appreciate it.

122
00:10:16.458 --> 00:10:19.375
Wasabi is a very bold ingredient.

123
00:10:19.458 --> 00:10:21.833
You love them or you hate them.

124
00:10:21.916 --> 00:10:24.458
But with the right balance

125
00:10:24.541 --> 00:10:28.958
will create a unique taste with which
no other ingredient compares.

126
00:10:29.458 --> 00:10:33.208
Regarding improvement, I want to make a suggestion

127
00:10:33.291 --> 00:10:36.166
changing the order of flavors.

128
00:10:36.250 --> 00:10:38.083
Be tasty.

129
00:10:38.666 --> 00:10:44.458
I will move the shy, hidden ones inside
wasabi filling on the outside.

130
00:10:47.458 --> 00:10:50.416
First, the tongue detects the spicy taste.

131
00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:53.208
Then it is covered with sweet chocolate,

132
00:10:53.791 --> 00:10:58.041
that makes it taste good
even gentler and sweeter.

133
00:11:01.500 --> 00:11:08.125
This way we will use extra
less wasabi than in the filling.

134
00:11:08.666 --> 00:11:10.375
That face again.

135
00:11:10.958 --> 00:11:11.791
What?

136
00:11:12.958 --> 00:11:15.083
You do it when you are happy.

137
00:11:17.458 --> 00:11:18.791
Did something good happen?

138
00:11:20.375 --> 00:11:21.625
I don't think so.

139
00:11:23.750 --> 00:11:25.166
It happened.

140
00:11:35.083 --> 00:11:35.916
All right.

141
00:11:38.250 --> 00:11:40.791
You can do it, Mr. Wasabi.

142
00:11:45.208 --> 00:11:46.041
PS.

143
00:11:47.166 --> 00:11:50.000
Like wasabi that came into the world,

144
00:11:50.083 --> 00:11:55.041
I hope so, too, someday
I'll meet everyone at Savior.

145
00:11:55.625 --> 00:11:57.750
An anonymous chocolatier.

146
00:12:27.041 --> 00:12:27.916
I'll try.

147
00:12:40.916 --> 00:12:42.083
And how?

148
00:13:14.250 --> 00:13:15.750
It's annoying.

149
00:13:19.416 --> 00:13:21.375
She's annoyingly good.

150
00:13:22.583 --> 00:13:24.750
For such an idea

151
00:13:25.583 --> 00:13:28.000
only a genius could come up with it.

152
00:13:28.916 --> 00:13:30.541
She really is better.

153
00:13:31.041 --> 00:13:33.541
I thought so too!

154
00:13:33.625 --> 00:13:35.958
First, wasabi bites the tongue.

155
00:13:36.041 --> 00:13:38.583
Then comes the sweetness of the chocolate.

156
00:13:38.666 --> 00:13:41.541
I could eat an infinite amount of them!

157
00:13:41.625 --> 00:13:45.291
The design screams "wasabi chocolate"
and it's even prettier.

158
00:13:45.375 --> 00:13:50.708
This one is good too
but I still prefer Boss Kenji's version.

159
00:13:51.208 --> 00:13:52.041
NO.

160
00:13:53.041 --> 00:13:55.958
This time I lost. I admit it.

161
00:13:56.041 --> 00:13:58.375
It's not about winning or losing.

162
00:13:59.500 --> 00:14:04.541
What matters is not to give up easily
and always strive for something better.

163
00:14:06.583 --> 00:14:12.416
So do we agree
for this new Wasabi en Soie?

164
00:14:13.958 --> 00:14:14.958
Yes.

165
00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:20.125
Starting tomorrow we use a new recipe.

166
00:14:20.208 --> 00:14:21.208
Yes, boss.

167
00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:24.041
- Let's compare them.
- Great.

168
00:14:24.125 --> 00:14:26.125
This might sell well.

169
00:14:28.125 --> 00:14:29.375
Good job.

170
00:14:30.208 --> 00:14:33.041
I thought you wouldn't agree.
All bossy.

171
00:14:35.333 --> 00:14:37.000
Speaking of which, our boss…

172
00:14:38.458 --> 00:14:41.750
I don't think he ever came out before us.

173
00:14:42.666 --> 00:14:45.583
Do you think he feels the same as us?

174
00:14:46.083 --> 00:14:47.500
It's hard to say.

175
00:14:47.583 --> 00:14:49.708
Who knows what he's thinking behind the scenes?

176
00:14:52.500 --> 00:14:55.208
Okay, this needs to be celebrated.

177
00:14:55.291 --> 00:14:58.625
Shall we have a drink? This hasn't happened for a long time!

178
00:14:59.208 --> 00:15:01.416
I'm exhausted.

179
00:15:01.500 --> 00:15:04.166
That's why I have to go for a drink!

180
00:15:04.250 --> 00:15:05.708
It's the same again.

181
00:15:06.333 --> 00:15:08.791
They will use any excuse to drink.

182
00:15:08.875 --> 00:15:11.708
I heard it. Show respect to elders.

183
00:15:11.791 --> 00:15:12.958
Bright.

184
00:15:13.041 --> 00:15:16.000
Nowa, you're coming with us.
It is also a welcome party.

185
00:15:16.083 --> 00:15:19.666
I think I'll give up today.

186
00:15:19.750 --> 00:15:20.666
Why?

187
00:15:22.041 --> 00:15:26.208
On such a day we must raise a toast!

188
00:15:26.291 --> 00:15:27.375
Join us.

189
00:15:27.458 --> 00:15:30.166
- Let's go.
- Yes! All together!

190
00:15:31.250 --> 00:15:32.625
Today I will sing!

191
00:15:35.125 --> 00:15:36.083
Are you okay?

192
00:16:05.458 --> 00:16:07.458
Let's sit down. Who's sitting where?

193
00:16:14.958 --> 00:16:16.375
I'll sit here.

194
00:16:16.458 --> 00:16:17.500
Thanks.

195
00:16:17.583 --> 00:16:20.708
I'll have a drink at the bar.

196
00:16:36.541 --> 00:16:37.541
Revelation!

197
00:16:37.625 --> 00:16:39.958
Thank you very much!

198
00:16:40.041 --> 00:16:41.375
And now

199
00:16:41.458 --> 00:16:47.208
I'd like to pass the microphone
newest friend, Ms. Lee Hana!

200
00:16:47.291 --> 00:16:49.166
- NO!
- Please?

201
00:16:49.250 --> 00:16:50.083
No way!

202
00:16:50.166 --> 00:16:53.666
- We want to hear you sing!
- I really can't.

203
00:16:55.500 --> 00:16:56.458
I can't.

204
00:16:57.625 --> 00:16:58.583
You sing!

205
00:16:58.666 --> 00:16:59.750
All right?

206
00:17:01.208 --> 00:17:02.416
I'm fine.

207
00:17:02.500 --> 00:17:05.083
No, I've had enough.

208
00:17:05.166 --> 00:17:08.583
Do you want me to play something?

209
00:17:11.000 --> 00:17:14.125
We're just getting started. Next!

210
00:17:14.208 --> 00:17:18.041
Do you know any Japanese songs?

211
00:17:18.125 --> 00:17:19.333
You can do it, Hana!

212
00:17:19.416 --> 00:17:21.750
Not I. Nowadays she is a star.

213
00:17:21.833 --> 00:17:22.958
I'll try.

214
00:17:24.791 --> 00:17:25.625
All right.

215
00:17:28.333 --> 00:17:29.625
I'll try!

216
00:17:34.583 --> 00:17:35.750
Hanaka!

217
00:18:03.083 --> 00:18:10.083
As I walk, I look up

218
00:18:10.708 --> 00:18:17.708
So that my tears won't flow

219
00:18:18.416 --> 00:18:25.166
Remembering those spring days

220
00:18:25.666 --> 00:18:31.000
But today I'm all alone

221
00:18:34.750 --> 00:18:37.333
- He has a beautiful voice.
- Yes.

222
00:18:43.583 --> 00:18:46.208
I want to tell you all something.

223
00:18:48.250 --> 00:18:49.291
I am…

224
00:18:52.708 --> 00:18:54.250
Actually, I…

225
00:19:19.000 --> 00:19:20.541
Hey, look at me!

226
00:19:22.791 --> 00:19:24.875
- Mr. Fujiwara?
- This is Mr. Fujiwara.

227
00:19:26.416 --> 00:19:27.583
Listen.

228
00:19:27.666 --> 00:19:32.458
Don't you think it's a bit rude
for someone to sing unprepared?

229
00:19:35.041 --> 00:19:36.041
Sorry.

230
00:19:36.708 --> 00:19:38.541
What possessed him to come here?

231
00:19:39.125 --> 00:19:40.125
What not?

232
00:19:42.125 --> 00:19:44.500
I want to announce something important.

233
00:19:44.583 --> 00:19:46.375
You can sit down now.

234
00:19:46.875 --> 00:19:48.291
All right.

235
00:19:49.750 --> 00:19:50.791
All right.

236
00:19:51.291 --> 00:19:52.125
Is she okay?

237
00:19:53.291 --> 00:19:56.583
Microphone control. Test, one, two.

238
00:19:56.666 --> 00:19:58.541
Sorry to disturb you.

239
00:19:58.625 --> 00:20:02.541
I have a very important announcement.

240
00:20:07.375 --> 00:20:10.666
For today's drinks

241
00:20:11.166 --> 00:20:12.583
I'll pay!

242
00:20:30.833 --> 00:20:33.291
Please. Let me know if that's not enough.

243
00:20:34.458 --> 00:20:36.708
I wonder if Hana is okay.

244
00:20:38.500 --> 00:20:42.166
Damn, every employee is happy
it's quite a grind.

245
00:20:42.250 --> 00:20:43.083
For now.

246
00:20:51.333 --> 00:20:52.625
Everything's all right?

247
00:20:53.291 --> 00:20:54.583
I'm fine.

248
00:20:55.666 --> 00:20:57.333
It doesn't look like it.

249
00:20:57.416 --> 00:20:59.666
Please leave me alone!

250
00:20:59.750 --> 00:21:01.875
Why are you following me?

251
00:21:01.958 --> 00:21:03.916
I have a huge and durable umbrella.

252
00:21:04.000 --> 00:21:06.916
And you went all this way to show it off?

253
00:21:08.625 --> 00:21:09.833
Please hide.

254
00:21:09.916 --> 00:21:11.333
I'm fine!

255
00:21:11.416 --> 00:21:13.375
Please leave me!

256
00:21:18.666 --> 00:21:19.916
Are you crying?

257
00:21:22.958 --> 00:21:24.958
I'm just wet from the rain.

258
00:21:28.666 --> 00:21:30.875
What did you want to say earlier?

259
00:21:38.166 --> 00:21:39.166
Are you ma'am?

260
00:21:40.541 --> 00:21:42.791
Is he afraid of people looking at you?

261
00:21:45.916 --> 00:21:47.541
Is it possible…

262
00:21:50.333 --> 00:21:52.791
that only with me you feel good?

263
00:21:56.125 --> 00:21:57.208
I have the same thing.

264
00:22:00.708 --> 00:22:02.291
I…

265
00:22:05.125 --> 00:22:07.333
I can't touch anyone.

266
00:22:08.916 --> 00:22:09.750
But…

267
00:22:12.958 --> 00:22:14.750
I can only give you one lady.

268
00:22:16.083 --> 00:22:17.875
For some reason only Mrs.

269
00:22:38.375 --> 00:22:39.666
Please take it.

270
00:22:42.791 --> 00:22:45.875
I can't let
that my employee catches a cold.

271
00:22:57.583 --> 00:22:58.958
But no!

272
00:22:59.041 --> 00:23:00.000
I hate getting wet!

273
00:23:00.791 --> 00:23:02.583
- All right?
- NO.

274
00:23:02.666 --> 00:23:05.125
Can you walk home in the rain?

275
00:23:05.208 --> 00:23:06.583
- What?
- Oh no.

276
00:23:06.666 --> 00:23:09.541
I really can't! Sorry!

277
00:23:09.625 --> 00:23:10.541
What?

278
00:23:17.791 --> 00:23:19.208
Seriously…

279
00:23:52.041 --> 00:23:53.333
What happened?

280
00:23:54.666 --> 00:23:56.041
Are you okay?

281
00:23:58.750 --> 00:23:59.958
Do you…

282
00:24:01.416 --> 00:24:02.500
was he crying?

283
00:24:03.000 --> 00:24:04.875
I'm just wet from the rain.

284
00:24:06.958 --> 00:24:09.958
You are a conscientious person,
that she followed me here.

285
00:24:10.458 --> 00:24:13.166
I was worried
that you might have fainted on the way.

286
00:24:14.125 --> 00:24:16.291
That's why I ran after you.

287
00:24:16.958 --> 00:24:20.750
I was ready to call an ambulance
if you fainted in the rain.

288
00:24:22.833 --> 00:24:23.666
But…

289
00:24:25.083 --> 00:24:28.000
I know you want to be left alone.

290
00:24:45.375 --> 00:24:47.583
Since mom died

291
00:24:48.958 --> 00:24:52.916
I avoid eye contact with people.

292
00:24:54.250 --> 00:24:56.458
It didn't bother me at all.

293
00:24:58.708 --> 00:25:02.250
But sometimes I'm tired of always running away.

294
00:25:03.958 --> 00:25:07.041
I swore to myself
that this time I will try.

295
00:25:09.500 --> 00:25:10.875
Like before?

296
00:25:13.458 --> 00:25:14.708
Yes.

297
00:25:18.750 --> 00:25:23.583
I thought it was a little better
but nothing has changed.

298
00:25:26.750 --> 00:25:28.500
I'm not asking for much.

299
00:25:31.041 --> 00:25:33.583
I just want to look at the person
that I like, face to face.

300
00:25:38.541 --> 00:25:41.458
Is there anyone
Who do you feel this way about?

301
00:25:45.541 --> 00:25:46.458
Yes.

302
00:25:52.000 --> 00:25:52.833
Great.

303
00:25:53.500 --> 00:25:54.375
Just…

304
00:25:56.416 --> 00:26:00.375
I want to be with the person I like
look him in the eye

305
00:26:01.500 --> 00:26:04.458
laugh together, cry together...

306
00:26:06.333 --> 00:26:07.750
I just wish I could

307
00:26:09.125 --> 00:26:11.375
be able to do this.

308
00:26:13.041 --> 00:26:14.541
I think I understand.

309
00:26:16.916 --> 00:26:19.000
I can't do many things either.

310
00:26:19.541 --> 00:26:23.958
Like fooling around with friends
putting your arm around them

311
00:26:24.041 --> 00:26:25.375
or a high five.

312
00:26:27.958 --> 00:26:29.291
Same

313
00:26:31.125 --> 00:26:33.333
I wanted to be able to shake someone's hand.

314
00:26:34.875 --> 00:26:39.458
But everyone thinks
that I'm just a terrible germphobe.

315
00:26:43.500 --> 00:26:44.666
I…

316
00:26:47.458 --> 00:26:49.750
I don't think people are dirty.

317
00:26:52.666 --> 00:26:53.666
Except…

318
00:26:58.541 --> 00:27:00.041
I'm the dirty one.

319
00:27:00.791 --> 00:27:01.625
Yes.

320
00:27:24.541 --> 00:27:26.166
I think…

321
00:27:29.625 --> 00:27:32.458
that I'm too dirty
to touch anyone.

322
00:27:36.833 --> 00:27:37.833
That's why

323
00:27:39.625 --> 00:27:43.916
I felt comfortable
during the coronavirus pandemic.

324
00:27:46.458 --> 00:27:49.000
Everyone in the world was like me

325
00:27:50.166 --> 00:27:52.041
they avoided physical contact.

326
00:27:55.750 --> 00:28:00.208
But… it also made me sad.

327
00:28:01.291 --> 00:28:06.625
What was a nightmare for the world
for me it was happiness.

328
00:28:08.458 --> 00:28:12.666
I wonder why we're okay

329
00:28:14.083 --> 00:28:15.125
between us.

330
00:28:16.250 --> 00:28:17.250
I have no idea.

331
00:28:21.458 --> 00:28:22.791
Maybe

332
00:28:23.750 --> 00:28:24.958
are we soul mates?

333
00:28:25.041 --> 00:28:26.541
It's impossible.

334
00:28:26.625 --> 00:28:27.708
Right.

335
00:28:32.333 --> 00:28:38.500
But maybe... there's a reason for it.

336
00:28:38.583 --> 00:28:39.875
Reason?

337
00:28:39.958 --> 00:28:43.833
Maybe we can help each other.

338
00:28:43.916 --> 00:28:45.458
Help each other?

339
00:28:49.625 --> 00:28:51.583
Let's try to practice.

340
00:28:52.500 --> 00:28:53.916
It's like being in rehab.

341
00:28:55.458 --> 00:28:59.208
Let's touch and connect
eye contact if we can.

342
00:28:59.791 --> 00:29:01.250
Let's do it.

343
00:29:05.541 --> 00:29:06.416
But…

344
00:29:06.916 --> 00:29:10.583
That would be a problem
if it made you fall in love with me.

345
00:29:11.166 --> 00:29:13.750
No way. This will never happen.

346
00:29:14.583 --> 00:29:15.458
Yes.

347
00:29:16.666 --> 00:29:20.333
We can exercise.

348
00:29:22.333 --> 00:29:26.000
Well, I wouldn't fall in love with you either.

349
00:29:27.625 --> 00:29:28.458
Yes.

350
00:29:30.500 --> 00:29:31.875
All right.

351
00:29:34.625 --> 00:29:35.875
Let's try.

352
00:29:45.458 --> 00:29:46.708
I want to change.

353
00:29:47.791 --> 00:29:48.791
Really.

354
00:29:57.333 --> 00:29:58.541
All right.

355
00:30:03.708 --> 00:30:04.666
Let's practice.

356
00:30:14.250 --> 00:30:15.208
Let's practice.

357
00:30:31.125 --> 00:30:32.375
Sorry.

358
00:30:32.458 --> 00:30:33.750
NO.

359
00:30:35.708 --> 00:30:36.958
Never mind.

360
00:30:39.541 --> 00:30:41.666
We're just practicing.

361
00:30:43.791 --> 00:30:44.875
We exercise.

362
00:30:45.916 --> 00:30:46.750
Yes.

363
00:32:40.291 --> 00:32:41.125
Yes.

364
00:32:51.500 --> 00:32:52.666
Let's get better.

365
00:32:54.375 --> 00:32:55.250
Together.

366
00:33:33.083 --> 00:33:38.250
He perfected Kenji's recipe,
to increase sales.

367
00:33:39.500 --> 00:33:42.041
I guess he's already become a businessman.

368
00:33:44.666 --> 00:33:46.583
But he should stop slacking off

369
00:33:47.833 --> 00:33:50.291
and focus on getting the recipes.

370
00:33:51.375 --> 00:33:56.208
Shop chocolates
they have to come out in the second half of the year.

371
00:33:57.333 --> 00:34:00.708
Get other recipes quickly
and report to me.

372
00:34:01.833 --> 00:34:02.666
Yes Sir.

373
00:34:03.583 --> 00:34:05.375
When they lose their value,

374
00:34:06.708 --> 00:34:09.416
we will eliminate them.

375
00:34:13.416 --> 00:34:15.250
So you are going to close...

376
00:34:17.666 --> 00:34:18.833
Savior.

377
00:38:06.208 --> 00:38:09.041
Subtitles: Grzegorz Marczyk

